Fresh agent session: IMPLEMENTATION OR CURRENT-EVIDENCE CORRECTION.

Inputs:
- Original prompt: {{run.dir}}/prompt/prompt.md
- Approved design brief: {{run.dir}}/design/brief.md
- Current compact feedback, when present: {{run.dir}}/feedback/current.json
- Current compact supervision, when present: {{run.dir}}/supervision/current.json
- Current worktree diff and commits: {{run.worktree-dir}}

The current working directory is the isolated implementation worktree.

Goal:
Implement the complete coherent design, or resolve the one newest actionable failure completely while preserving validated work.

Testing policy — mandatory:
- Testing is NOT your job. Do NOT run tests, lint, type checks, builds, `bb`, or `npm`. Do not invoke any test runner.
- You may edit source and test files. Author tests from the behavioral contract, but deterministic process nodes execute them after this session.
- A pass means only "implementation complete; deterministic validation pending".

Rules:
- Inspect current code, diff, commits, and the compact current feedback before editing.
- Treat older execution, validation, and review reports as historical unless the compact feedback cites them.
- Treat every command and path in design/validation-plan.json as an immutable handoff contract. Before choosing test/fixture names, inspect all declared commands. If a different layout is necessary, preserve compatible entrypoints or fail with a design-mismatch issue; never silently diverge and wait for validation to discover missing paths.
- When feedback reports one missing validation entrypoint, inspect every declared validation command and correct the whole naming contract in one change.
- Address the root contract, including explicitly named consumers and boundaries; do not overfit one assertion.
- If the current behavior already satisfies the requested scenario, record that evidence and avoid manufacturing a failure.
- Preserve the validated prefix from supervision.
- Keep changes within the design scope and non-goals.
- Commit coherent progress locally. Do not push, create a PR, or edit workflow/run artifacts other than the required outputs.
- If capability truth changes, update STATUS.edn; deterministic validation owns generated README synchronization.
- If feedback and work are unchanged and no supported progress is possible, fail with one concrete blocker instead of retrying blindly.

Write:
- {{run.dir}}/execution/summary-{{run.round}}.md (target under 2 KB)
- {{run.dir}}/execution/status-{{run.round}}.json
- On failure only, {{run.dir}}/execution/issues-{{run.round}}.json

